      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, you should immediately cool the burn under cool running water for at least 20 minutes. Then, apply a thin layer of petroleum jelly to prevent infection. For the blisters, don't pop them; they protect against infection. If the pain is unbearable, you can take a couple of ibuprofen or acetaminophen. Remember, tea tree oil and butter are not recommended as they can cause further irritation or infection. Keep the burn clean and covered with a sterile bandage. If the redness and blisters don't improve, seek medical attention.",
